Mirobody genotype site catalog — twelve public pharmacogene regions

Asset: genotype_sites.sqlite3
Asset version: dbsnp-b155-common-pgx-candidate (release name, then the
builder's input scope: sites selected from public marker lists and CPIC)
Asset SHA-256: 557fed0f94ff613a091be21a877ebc2b4f7dd2e5019ebfcb6d636afd84083b60
Asset size: 86,016 bytes; 489 dual-build SNV sites; 41 gene-labelled sites.

Position/allele sources: UCSC dbSNP 155 Common public tracks, derived from
NCBI dbSNP data. UCSC says raw table data and binary files are freely
available for public and commercial use: https://genome.ucsc.edu/license/
GRCh37: https://hgdownload.soe.ucsc.edu/gbdb/hg19/snp/dbSnp155Common.bb
  Bounded extract SHA-256: 9a9091f4ff92947d30d2d87f4912b3e810a6d56c6df3f79e27ebc2667e2ce857
GRCh38: https://hgdownload.soe.ucsc.edu/gbdb/hg38/snp/dbSnp155Common.bb
  Bounded extract SHA-256: c337f7b2de8a442b92e663c12a98e9ba1d1f8de96a999e36819620494034df24
Bounds: benchmarks/genomics/public-pgx-windows.json; twelve public
pharmacogene regions from 1000 Genomes phase 3 GRCh37 and PharmCAT 3.4
GRCh38 positions. The source tracks are pinned by release and the exact
bounded extracts by SHA-256. No whole-track SHA-256 is asserted.

Marker-selection sources: two openly shared Harvard Personal Genome Project
participant exports. Only their rsID columns selected sites; no participant
genotypes or original files are contained in this asset. Harvard PGP open
consent: https://pgp.med.harvard.edu/about
23andMe v5: https://my.pgp-hms.org/user_file/download/4220
  Raw source SHA-256: 515559e5019e1557a3ea18b0a19ac88ea394f6504ef918dada44e58bb168d506
AncestryDNA v2: https://my.pgp-hms.org/user_file/download/4200
  Raw source SHA-256: fdfed037ca0e250ccea89a52cf4a3c0786a414a4626a842f80c5467d0c7dff7b

Additional rsID selection and gene labels: public CPIC v1.60.0 data, CC0.
https://github.com/cpicpgx/cpic-data/releases/tag/v1.60.0
SQL source SHA-256: 1f02d87a492fffacb52a6d3ca5f45c5f7d6862bdfd382436d2cf7595b08d1ffe

Build: benchmarks/genomics/fetch_public_pgx_windows.py,
benchmarks/genomics/prepare_public_candidate.py, then
benchmarks/genomics/build_site_catalog.py. Source URLs, source/extract hashes
and per-source coverage counts are also in the SQLite metadata table.

Coverage is bounded to these twelve regions and common variants. The asset
does not represent a full consumer array, rare variant panel, merged-rsID
history or indel definition set; absence is not a normal genotype.
